1|// The LITMUS gate, reimplemented during the event from the published papers
2|// (Litmus: The Admissible Set, doi 10.5281/zenodo.21227402, and its
3|// architecture companion, doi 10.5281/zenodo.21227855). Not copied from writ.
4|//
5|// What the papers fix:
6|//   - The check is deterministic and sits outside the model. A model grading
7|//     a model is the weak litmus the paper names as the one that fell away.
8|//   - It fails closed. Nothing ungrounded leaves; the worst case is deferral.
9|//   - Chart grounding is a referential warrant: it verifies that the draft
10|//     says what the record says, not that the care was right. Judgment stays
11|//     with the physician, who sees criterion, quote, and sentence together.
12|//   - Every claim, gate decision, and verdict is recorded (the provenance layer).
13|//
14|// How this gate checks support (the part the papers leave to the builder):
15|//   1. Resolve the citation to one chart entry. Unknown or malformed: unresolved.
16|//   2. The quote must appear verbatim in that entry's text (whitespace, case,
17|//      quote glyphs, and dash variants normalized: curly quotes to straight,
18|//      en, em, and figure dashes and the minus sign to the ASCII hyphen;
19|//      nothing else). Absent or trivial: refuted.
20|//   3. Every hard token in the sentence (numbers, dates, codes, and a side,
21|//      left or right) must appear in the cited entry, the payer criteria,
22|//      the denial, or the stated case facts. Anything else: refuted, token named.
23|//      The whole cited entry counts, not only the quoted span: the gate exists
24|//      to catch invented facts, not to grade quoting form, and the clinician who
25|//      wrote the entry did not write it to a payer's vocabulary.
26|//   4. A check that throws is an error, never a refutation and never a pass.
27|// There is no resemblance threshold and no keyword list. The evidence is the
28|// clinician's own words, which no payer vocabulary can require.
29|import { sha256Hex } from './hash.js';
30|import { CITATION_ID } from './citation.js';
