45|A worked example of the form, with invented content. Chart entry note-004 reads: "Finished 12 weeks of PT across the street, says it helped while she was there and then right back to baseline." Criterion crit-2 reads: "At least 3 months of conservative treatment without adequate relief." Good evidence: {criterion: "crit-2", citation: "note-004", quote: "Finished 12 weeks of PT across the street, says it helped while she was there and then right back to baseline"}. Good sentence: {text: "The record documents twelve weeks of physical therapy without lasting relief, which exceeds the 3 months the policy requires.", citation: "note-004", quote: "Finished 12 weeks of PT across the street, says it helped while she was there and then right back to baseline"}. The sentence may translate PT into physical therapy and 12 weeks into twelve weeks; the quote may not. The 3 months comes from the criterion, so it is sourced. A sentence claiming 16 weeks would be blocked.`;
